course: dictionary
lesson: 13853
title: Jot: a quick note and a tiny bit
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some small words have more than one job. «Jot» can be a verb (an action) or a noun (a thing). Check the words around it to see which one it is. «Please jot down the date before you start.» Here jot down tells you to write something quickly, in a few words.
explain: «She did not change a jot of her plan.» In this sentence, jot is a noun, and it means a very tiny amount. Test your meaning in the sentence: she did not change even a tiny bit of her plan. That makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: The phrase «not a jot» means not at all. Words like this are often found in older stories and in the Bible. In UK schools, and especially in Scotland, a rough notebook is called a jotter, so a teacher may say, «Do your sums in your jotter first.»
fact: Jot can be a verb or a noun, so check the sentence to see which one it is.
fact: To jot something down means to write it quickly, in a few words.
fact: A jot is a very tiny amount.
fact: «Not a jot» means not at all, or not even the smallest bit.
fact: A jotter is a rough notebook, used in UK schools and especially in Scotland.
exercise: «Please jot down the date before you start.» What does jot down mean? | To forget it | To say it out loud very slowly | *To write it quickly in a few words | To draw a big picture of it
exercise: «He did not change a jot of his plan.» What does a jot mean here? | *A very tiny amount | A big, tall pile | A long journey | A loud noise
exercise: In Scotland, your teacher says, «Put your rough sums in your jotter.» What is a jotter? | A school bus | A kind of pencil case | *A rough notebook | A type of dinner
test: «She did not care a jot about the prize.» What does not care a jot mean? | Cared very, very much | *Did not care at all | Was too tired to think | Cared a little, but was still interested
test: Which sentence uses jot as a verb? | «Jot is a short word.» | «There was not a jot of milk left.» | «She bought a new jotter for school.» | *«I will jot these ideas on my notepad.»
exam: The teacher asked us to ___ down our ideas before we start writing. | *jot | joke | jolt | jotter
